Invent Yourself scripsit:

> And, to confirm, in your opinion, these Lojban sentences are actually
> identical in meaning?
> 
> ca ro djedi lo nanmu cu cinba la meris
> lo nanmu ca ro djedi cu cinba la meris

No, I hold that they mean "Concurrent with each day, there exists a man/men
who kiss(es) Mary" and "There exists a man/men who concurrent with each day
kiss(es) Mary". The first one is consistent with different kissers on
different days, whereas the second one is not.

